d absence in the mount, they were ready to transfer their allegiance from Jehovah to some of the divinities to whose worship they had previously been accustomed. The worship of cattle was especially common, as of Apis at Memphis and Mnevis at Heliopolis.-G. B. S."},{"id":"00eeb00c6bfa","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":17,"p":[2,2],"r":[20,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"It is not probable that this passage (v. 39, 40) means that the people proposed to return to Egypt (as Chrys.). In the O. T. the constant representation is that the golden calf (or bull) was worshipped as the image of the divinity who had led them out of Egypt (Ex. xxxii. 4; 1 Kings xii. 28). It seems clearly implied in Ezek. xx. 7, Ezek. xx. 8, Ezek. xx. 24, that the Israelites while in Egypt had been much addicted to the idolatry of the country. The meaning here is that, being discouraged and disappointed on account of Moses' continued absence in the mount, they were ready to transfer their allegiance from Jehovah to some of the divinities to whose worship they had previously been accustomed. The worship of cattle was especially common, as of Apis at Memphis and Mnevis at Heliopolis.-G. B. S."},{"id":"c45c4f7995d3","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":17,"p":[2,2],"r":[20,24],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"It is not probable that this passage (v. 39, 40) means that the people proposed to return to Egypt (as Chrys.). In the O. T. the constant representation is that the golden calf (or bull) was worshipped as the image of the divinity who had led them out of Egypt (Ex. xxxii. 4; 1 Kings xii. 28). It seems clearly implied in Ezek. xx. 7, Ezek. xx. 8, Ezek. xx. 24, that the Israelites while in Egypt had been much addicted to the idolatry of the country. The meaning here is that, being discouraged and disappointed on account of Moses' continued absence in the mount, they were ready to transfer their allegiance from Jehovah to some of the divinities to whose worship they had previously been accustomed. The worship of cattle was especially common, as of Apis at Memphis and Mnevis at Heliopolis.-G. B. S."},{"id":"d227c6506e98","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":17,"p":[2,2],"r":[20,25],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Ezek. xx. 25"},{"id":"b40e361a8d93","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":43,"p":[3,3],"r":[16,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Ezek. xvi. 2"},{"id":"ff79f10497cc","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_act","w":"chrysostomus.hom_act","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":43,"p":[3,3],"r":[9,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Ezek. ix. 8"},{"id":"df5bd6864d8c","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":23,"p":[22,22],"r":[16,37,16,42],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Ezek. xvi. 37-42"},{"id":"6d383109f49c","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":29,"p":[23,23],"r":[34,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Ezek. xxxiv. 2"},{"id":"9f1ae88dd27f","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_1co","w":"chrysostomus.hom_1co","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":29,"p":[10,10],"r":[3,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Ezekiel chapter 3, verse 15"},{"id":"5eb14b4d21a2","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_1co","w":"chrysostomus.hom_1co","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":33,"p":[30,30],"r":[9,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Ezekiel chapter 9, verse 8"},{"id":"33b9acea1faa","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_1co","w":"chrysostomus.hom_1co","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":39,"p":[82,82],"r":[16,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Ezekiel chapter 16, ve